```
from typing import Literal
```

~Reply(message: str, status: Literal["approved", "pending"])

> profile: policy_reviewer:
  > model: `judge_model`

@draft(note: str) -> Reply:
  >> Convert this internal support note into a brief customer-facing reply: <note>
  Preserve the status stated in the note. The reply is [reply: Reply].
  = `reply`

@review(reply: Reply) -> bool:
  > use: policy_reviewer
  >> The authoritative policy is <policy>. The proposed customer reply is <<reply>>.
  Its status and message are [supported: Annotated[bool, "Are the reply's status and message supported by the authoritative policy, without claiming an approval that has not happened?"]].
  = `supported`

@revise(reply: Reply) -> Reply:
  >> Correct this customer reply <<reply>> using the authoritative policy <policy>.
  Do not claim completed approval. The corrected reply is [corrected: Reply].
  = `corrected`

@respond(note: str) -> dict:
  [first: Reply] = `draft(note)`
  [accepted: bool] = `review(first)`
  > if: `accepted`:
    = `dict(first=first.model_dump(), final=first.model_dump(), initial_accepted=accepted, final_accepted=accepted, revisions=0)`
  > else:
    [corrected: Reply] = `revise(first)`
    [final_accepted: bool] = `review(corrected)`
    = `dict(first=first.model_dump(), final=corrected.model_dump(), initial_accepted=accepted, final_accepted=final_accepted, revisions=1)`

= `respond(note)`
